# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.14.2 - Provide protection from malicious code
# Platform: M365 (Intune compliance policies)
# Check type: m365_graph_query against /deviceManagement/deviceCompliancePolicies

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-14-2-m365-malicious-code-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `m365`
    criticality `high`

    title `CMMC L1 SI.L1-3.14.2: Provide protection from malicious code`
    description `Validates that at least one device compliance policy is published. Compliance policies are the mechanism Intune uses to require malicious-code protection (antivirus, real-time scanning, signature freshness) as a precondition for device compliance.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `m365,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-14-2,si,malicious-code,intune,defender`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.14.2`
    control_objective `3.14.2`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `M365:tenant:endpoint-management`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Publish at least one Intune device compliance policy requiring antivirus / Defender enabled and active. The policy must be assigned to in-scope device groups so non-compliant devices fail the compliance evaluation and are blocked from accessing organizational resources via Conditional Access.`

    component_id `comp-m365-endpoint`

    impl_3_14_2 `Endpoints in the boundary are protected from malicious code by a centrally managed antimalware solution whose enabled and active state is enforced by device compliance policy. The compliance policy fails any device that lacks active antimalware protection; Conditional Access then prevents non-compliant devices from accessing organizational resources, creating a hard gate against any endpoint with malware protection disabled or absent. Real-time scanning is included in the compliance requirement, ensuring detection occurs continuously rather than only at scheduled intervals.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT compliance_policies
        path `deviceManagement/deviceCompliancePolicies`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliance_policy_published
        found boolean = true
        record
            field rows.*.id string != `` at_least_one
            field rows.*.displayName string != `` at_least_one
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN m365_graph_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliance_policy_published
            OBJECT_REF compliance_policies
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
